    "fridge": "Discard refrigerated perishable food such as meat, poultry, fish, eggs, and leftovers after 4 hours without power.",
    "fridgeHeadline": "your refrigerator will keep food safe for up to 4 hours during a power outage. Keep the door closed as much as possible.",
    "chartColumn": "Exposed to temperatures of 40°F (4°C) or above for more than 2 hours",
    "freezer": "A full freezer will hold a safe temperature for approximately 48 hours (24 hours if it is half full and the door remains closed).",
    "refreeze": "Food may be safely refrozen if it still contains ice crystals or is at 40°F (4°C) or below, however, its quality may suffer.",
    "mayo": "Opened mayonnaise, tartar sauce, horseradish (if above 50°F (10°C) for more than 8 hrs)",
    "frozenVeg": "Discard after held above 40°F (4°C) for 6 hours",
    "doubt": "When in Doubt, Throw it Out!",
    "neverTaste": "After a power outage never taste food to determine its safety."
